ROOT CAUSE (two concurrent faults)
  1. STALE PORT
     ~/.ssh/config had   Port 54257   (from previous Connect session)
     Workspace now on    Port 50274
     Verified: nc 127.0.0.1 50274 -> OPEN ; nc 127.0.0.1 54257 -> CLOSED

  2. REVOKED KEY
     Key file was well-formed (valid OPENSSH PRIVATE KEY, ed25519, 0600)
     but rejected by the server. Per CloudIDE docs:
       "One key per connection: it is replaced on the next Connect and
        revoked when the workspace stops."
     Key comment showed an older session UUID:
       cloudide-8b8722f0-5669-4c66-8ddb-8790d7c7f731
     No fresh download was present in ~/Downloads.

RESOLUTION
  1. cp ~/.ssh/config ~/.ssh/config.bak
  2. sed -i '' 's/Port 54257/Port 50274/' ~/.ssh/config
  3. Download key again from CloudIDE page -> ~/Downloads/cloudide-8b8722f0
  4. cp ~/Downloads/cloudide-8b8722f0 ~/.ssh/cloudide-8b8722f0
  5. chmod 600 ~/.ssh/cloudide-8b8722f0
  6. ssh -o BatchMode=yes cloudide-8b8722f0  -> SUCCESS

